/-!
# R005 — groups whose composition factors are all isomorphic to one simple group

The structural layer: if every composition factor of `G` is isomorphic to a fixed simple
group `S` (formalized as the extension closure `CompFactorsIso S G`), then `I(G)` lies in
the monoid generated by `I(S)`, `𝒥(G) ≤ 1 + Λ`, and any reciprocal-mass bound below `1`
gives `𝒥(G) < 2`, hence HS — `HSC.isHS_of_compFactors` and, with the uniform Euler-product
bound of `HSC.massBound_euler`, `HSC.isHS_of_compFactors_of_euler`.

The `A₅` instance is unconditional (`HSC.HS_of_compFactors_Alt5`), and `A₅` is exactly the
case where the uniform Euler product fails to be `< 2` (`HSC.euler_a5_gt_two`).  The
per-simple-group index data for the rest of the classification is *not* formalized: this
development reduces that layer to one numeric inequality per `S`.

Corresponds to <https://stepsunbounded.com/results/R005/>.
-/
